WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.847 --> 00:00:03.250
A large plant is building a new hall.

2
00:00:03.954 --> 00:00:07.217
Line 3 has to move there, during the summer shutdown.

3
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.201
You start as a consultant and the sponsor asks, move line 3.

4
00:00:13.177 --> 00:00:16.973
Before the intake begins, you choose how to run the project.

5
00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:20.460
We follow this request through four topics.

6
00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:24.459
Two are about how you work, and two about what you work with.

7
00:00:25.785 --> 00:00:29.059
The first topic is The route, what first and what next.

8
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:32.403
How does a project run from start to finish?

9
00:00:33.428 --> 00:00:37.492
A project runs over five stages, from intake to close.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.204
Each stage leaves one stage product that the next one needs.

11
00:00:43.005 --> 00:00:45.502
Like an assignment, a plan or a decision.

12
00:00:46.557 --> 00:00:48.055
It starts with a mandate.

13
00:00:48.823 --> 00:00:51.656
That is the authority to start, from the sponsor.

14
00:00:52.714 --> 00:00:56.696
If you take over a running project, you first do a status check.

15
00:00:58.001 --> 00:01:00.416
The second topic is Choosing an approach.

16
00:01:01.182 --> 00:01:03.504
Which way of working fits this project?

17
00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:07.023
There are four method families and a mix.

18
00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.641
Predictive, agile, Lean and Six Sigma.

19
00:01:11.672 --> 00:01:13.088
The move is predictive.

20
00:01:13.792 --> 00:01:15.406
Plan first, then run.

21
00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:21.165
A recurring problem with data you tackle with DMAIC, the steps of Six Sigma.

22
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:24.712
The third topic is Choosing tools.

23
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.184
Which tool do you pick, and when does it pay off?

24
00:01:29.239 --> 00:01:32.281
A tool pays off when it yields more than it costs.

25
00:01:33.284 --> 00:01:37.127
Think in tool families, one kind of tool for each kind of work.

26
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.992
One for lists, one for schedules.

27
00:01:41.031 --> 00:01:43.632
We put the tasks of the move on a task board.

28
00:01:44.936 --> 00:01:48.198
The fourth topic is Tools at large organisations.

29
00:01:48.929 --> 00:01:51.634
The client is large and has many systems.

30
00:01:52.665 --> 00:01:57.367
Each system has one task, such as hours and money, projects or drawings.

31
00:01:58.405 --> 00:02:02.236
A system of record is the system where a fact is officially kept.

32
00:02:03.287 --> 00:02:05.307
The planner gives you the project code.

33
00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:08.311
Under it you book hours in the ERP.

34
00:02:09.597 --> 00:02:11.281
This is the map of Projects.

35
00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.959
Approach and tools is the first station on the road of a project.

36
00:02:16.995 --> 00:02:20.559
Approach and tools has four topics, each with four levels.

37
00:02:21.565 --> 00:02:23.771
Start with The route, at Basics level.

38
00:02:24.831 --> 00:02:28.220
At Working knowledge you take over a project, apply a method,

39
00:02:28.383 --> 00:02:30.821
set up your tools and work as a guest.

40
00:02:31.878 --> 00:02:33.503
At Advanced you tailor the route,

41
00:02:33.643 --> 00:02:36.917
choose method and tools and decide what lives where.

42
00:02:37.948 --> 00:02:40.247
At Expert you work in the client’s route,

43
00:02:40.397 --> 00:02:43.265
weigh what tools cost and oversee the landscape.

44
00:02:44.304 --> 00:02:47.218
After that comes the intake, the second station.
